From: pmOS Mi8Lite <macosmojave2@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm660: mux Secondary MI2S pins on platina

The TFA9894 speaker is fed by Secondary MI2S; without muxing gpio24-27 to the
sec_mi2s function the amp receives no bit clock and stays silent. Add the pin
state and apply it via the sound card.

Signed-off-by: pmOS Mi8Lite <macosmojave2@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm660-xiaomi-platina.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm660-xiaomi-platina.dts
@@ -1144,3 +1144,18 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/* Secondary MI2S pins (SCK/WS/SD) to the TFA9894 speaker amp. Without this the
+ * amp gets no bit clock (NOCLK) and stays silent. */
+&tlmm {
+	sec_mi2s_default: sec-mi2s-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio24", "gpio25", "gpio26", "gpio27";
+		function = "sec_mi2s";
+		drive-strength = <8>;
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+};
+
+&sound {
+	pinctrl-0 = <&cdc_pdm_default>, <&cdc_dmic_default>, <&sec_mi2s_default>;
+};
